# Sample Package Manifest

File: ooda/opm/examples/manifest.oot

A minimal package manifest declares the package's name, version, capabilities, and dependencies.

```
name: hello-world
version: 1.2.3
caps: [&FsReadCap, &FsWriteCap, &NetCap]
deps:
  - name: json-parser
    version: ^2.0.0
  - name: http-client
    version: ~1.5.0
checksum: sha256:9f86d081884c7d659a2feaa0c55ad015a3bf4f1b2b0b822cd15d6c15b0f00a08
```

## Field Semantics

- `name`: unique package name (lowercase, hyphenated).
- `version`: Semantic Version (major.minor.patch).
- `caps`: the granular capability tokens the package needs.
- `deps`: list of {name, version-range, checksum} entries.
- `checksum`: SHA-256 of the package tarball, verified at install time.
